No.

00:10:51.340 --> 00:10:52.608
But she said,

00:10:52.608 --> 00:10:54.518
"I really doubt that I
held y'all in from recess

00:10:54.518 --> 00:10:57.598
'cause I've never done
that as a punishment,"

00:10:57.598 --> 00:10:59.809
and we were like,

00:10:59.809 --> 00:11:00.642
well.

00:11:00.642 --> 00:11:01.630
We're gonna edit this out.

00:11:01.630 --> 00:11:02.565
Yeah, yeah.
Is what we were thinking.

00:11:02.565 --> 00:11:04.214
But I-
Wasn't gonna document.

00:11:04.214 --> 00:11:05.523
But I was like ...

00:11:05.523 --> 00:11:06.356
But I know.

00:11:06.356 --> 00:11:08.030
But like I believe that to be true, like.

00:11:08.030 --> 00:11:08.863
Yeah.

00:11:08.863 --> 00:11:09.708
And that was a...

00:11:09.708 --> 00:11:13.289
There's memories pre being a nasty word,

00:11:13.289 --> 00:11:14.456
public figure.

00:11:15.308 --> 00:11:17.352
Like, you know,

00:11:17.352 --> 00:11:19.550
when you have to like
answer questions by people,

00:11:19.550 --> 00:11:21.773
reporters and stuff like that

00:11:21.773 --> 00:11:22.854
or you're simplifying things

00:11:22.854 --> 00:11:25.412
and you're an entertainment act,

00:11:25.412 --> 00:11:27.475
at that point all bets are off.

00:11:27.475 --> 00:11:28.780
You're gonna like massage things

00:11:28.780 --> 00:11:30.348
and you're gonna tell the big fish story

00:11:30.348 --> 00:11:32.099
and the story's gonna be this big.

00:11:32.099 --> 00:11:34.757
But back before when I was just
remembering things on my own

00:11:34.757 --> 00:11:36.073
and we were remembering things as friends-

00:11:36.073 --> 00:11:36.906
Right.

00:11:36.906 --> 00:11:39.160
I was 100% sure that we
were held in from recess.

00:11:39.160 --> 00:11:39.993
Yeah, we were-

00:11:39.993 --> 00:11:40.826
And we were coloring.

00:11:40.826 --> 00:11:43.155
We were doing some
interviews for local papers

00:11:43.155 --> 00:11:46.229
but it was, you know, and we were...

00:11:46.229 --> 00:11:49.475
Maybe there was a temptation
to massage the story

00:11:49.475 --> 00:11:52.558
for the documentary or to simplify it

00:11:53.859 --> 00:11:56.442
but no, we absolutely believed.

00:11:57.418 --> 00:11:59.292
I cannot remember, I don't have...

00:11:59.292 --> 00:12:02.375
I cannot visualize getting in trouble

00:12:03.588 --> 00:12:07.877
but I know in my heart of hearts
that we did get in trouble.

00:12:07.877 --> 00:12:12.435
But I'm 100% sure this
is something I would

00:12:12.435 --> 00:12:14.340
bet everything on.

00:12:14.340 --> 00:12:16.948
We were not being held in from
recess for writing profanity

00:12:16.948 --> 00:12:17.859
on our desks.

00:12:17.859 --> 00:12:18.740
We were-
Okay, but

00:12:18.740 --> 00:12:21.049
we believed we were
being held in from recess

00:12:21.049 --> 00:12:22.844
even though Ms. Locklear said she didn't-

00:12:22.844 --> 00:12:23.677
I believe that.

00:12:23.677 --> 00:12:24.510
She never did that.

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:25.343
I believe that she did that.

00:12:25.343 --> 00:12:26.176
So it's like,

00:12:26.176 --> 00:12:27.225
if we weren't held in from recess,

00:12:27.225 --> 00:12:29.957
we were punished in some way that I think

00:12:29.957 --> 00:12:33.899
it might have been a
succinct way to say it was,

00:12:33.899 --> 00:12:34.893
we were held in from recess,

00:12:34.893 --> 00:12:38.233
that's a more visceral way to sit to...

00:12:38.233 --> 00:12:40.509
A picture to paint than just,

00:12:40.509 --> 00:12:43.701
"Oh, we were punished and
we had to color pictures",

00:12:43.701 --> 00:12:45.145
like the two of...

00:12:45.145 --> 00:12:49.895
The scene that everyone's
outdoors and we are in the room

00:12:51.485 --> 00:12:53.697
just the two of us,

00:12:53.697 --> 00:12:57.280
I am willing to say
that might not be true.

00:12:59.264 --> 00:13:01.918
Okay, but you glossed over something,

00:13:01.918 --> 00:13:05.205
Mr. Neil, you glossed over the pun...

00:13:05.205 --> 00:13:06.704
What we were being punished for,

00:13:06.704 --> 00:13:08.788
I'm saying I am 100%.

00:13:08.788 --> 00:13:10.248
Oh no, I'm saying that's the next thing.

00:13:10.248 --> 00:13:11.105
Out of whole cloth.

00:13:11.105 --> 00:13:11.938
Yeah.

00:13:11.938 --> 00:13:14.671
We made up the writing
profanity on our desks.

00:13:14.671 --> 00:13:15.635
We, and-

00:13:15.635 --> 00:13:16.728
For a while we said,

00:13:16.728 --> 00:13:17.886
we didn't remember what we wrote.

00:13:17.886 --> 00:13:18.743
Well, here's what we did.

00:13:18.743 --> 00:13:19.576
And then we just added what we did right.

00:13:19.576 --> 00:13:21.177
Here's what we did.

00:13:21.177 --> 00:13:22.144
I agree.

00:13:22.144 --> 00:13:23.318
We did not...

00:13:23.318 --> 00:13:25.679
I do not believe-
How do you feel right now?

00:13:25.679 --> 00:13:26.512
I do not believe-
Do you feel deceived?

00:13:26.512 --> 00:13:28.857
That we wrote profanity on our desk.

00:13:28.857 --> 00:13:29.690
'Cause we...

00:13:29.690 --> 00:13:30.914
Neither one of us would've ever done that.

00:13:30.914 --> 00:13:31.747
Not right.

00:13:31.747 --> 00:13:33.421
You wouldn't have defaced things-

00:13:33.421 --> 00:13:34.254
Hell no.

00:13:34.254 --> 00:13:35.664
Just out of personal principles.

00:13:35.664 --> 00:13:36.627
Damn no.

00:13:36.627 --> 00:13:38.183
I would not have defaced things

00:13:38.183 --> 00:13:40.589
out of fear of being
murdered by my parents.

00:13:40.589 --> 00:13:43.172
I have never defaced anything

00:13:44.218 --> 00:13:45.486
in a graffiti-esque type of way-

00:13:45.486 --> 00:13:46.353
Yeah.

00:13:46.353 --> 00:13:47.293
In my entire life.

00:13:47.293 --> 00:13:48.126
Yeah.

00:13:48.126 --> 00:13:48.959
I was...

00:13:48.959 --> 00:13:49.792
I mean.

00:13:49.792 --> 00:13:51.375
Like, I don't think I could
bring myself to do it now.

00:13:51.375 --> 00:13:53.298
I mean ironically, we invite people to do

00:13:53.298 --> 00:13:55.173
that when we had guests on Ear Biscuits.

00:13:55.173 --> 00:13:56.006
Oh, we yeah invited them.

00:13:56.006 --> 00:13:56.872
But it wasn't...

00:13:56.872 --> 00:13:57.989
You know, we invited them too.

00:13:57.989 --> 00:13:58.871
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:13:58.871 --> 00:13:59.704
But yeah.

00:13:59.704 --> 00:14:00.742
I've never done it and so-

00:14:00.742 --> 00:14:01.728
I would've never done it.

00:14:01.728 --> 00:14:03.208
100% confident that-

00:14:03.208 --> 00:14:04.190
That's made up.
I not do that,

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:05.940
but here's my defense

00:14:07.452 --> 00:14:08.452
for the lie.

00:14:10.098 --> 00:14:12.982
What we said at first was most likely

00:14:12.982 --> 00:14:15.431
something to the effect of...

00:14:15.431 --> 00:14:18.821
'Cause the reporter will
ask, well, you know,

00:14:18.821 --> 00:14:20.739
what were you...

00:14:20.739 --> 00:14:22.072
What did you do?

00:14:23.189 --> 00:14:24.758
And we're like, well we probably-

00:14:24.758 --> 00:14:25.749
Wrote some words on desk.

00:14:25.749 --> 00:14:27.781
Probably wrote something,

00:14:27.781 --> 00:14:28.614
probably write-
Just made something.

00:14:28.614 --> 00:14:29.447
Write on our desk.

00:14:29.447 --> 00:14:30.314
We'll say, "Oh we talked too much."

00:14:30.314 --> 00:14:33.174
I remember that the desks
had writing on them.

00:14:33.174 --> 00:14:34.381
From previous generations.

00:14:34.381 --> 00:14:36.299
From other people.

00:14:36.299 --> 00:14:38.172
And that is something
that you would've gotten

00:14:38.172 --> 00:14:39.005
in trouble for.

00:14:39.005 --> 00:14:40.147
I think that happened during the song,

00:14:40.147 --> 00:14:41.025
by the way, the song composition.

00:14:41.025 --> 00:14:45.497
I think we probably said
something like before the song,

00:14:45.497 --> 00:14:47.218
you know what,

00:14:47.218 --> 00:14:49.307
we were probably scribbling
on our desks like, oh,

00:14:49.307 --> 00:14:51.546
and then the reporter's like,
"What were you writing?"

00:14:51.546 --> 00:14:53.143
And we're like, "Well, we
gotta come up with something,"

00:14:53.143 --> 00:14:54.695
it's like, "Oh, I don't know.

00:14:54.695 --> 00:14:56.616
We might have been writing profanity."

00:14:56.616 --> 00:15:00.713
You know, it was probably just
like couched and hypothetical

00:15:00.713 --> 00:15:03.555
that then the next time we
told the story, it was like,

00:15:03.555 --> 00:15:04.388
you know what?

00:15:04.388 --> 00:15:06.528
That was a better story,

00:15:06.528 --> 00:15:09.226
we're gonna keep it
couched and hypothetical

00:15:09.226 --> 00:15:12.119
but we're gonna tell it more
succinctly and then over time

00:15:12.119 --> 00:15:15.480
the succinct ability of it
removes the hypothetical.

00:15:15.480 --> 00:15:16.313
Well, and I think...

00:15:16.313 --> 00:15:18.424
Here's my defense.
And then you write a song.

00:15:18.424 --> 00:15:22.382
Here's my defense of
how this happens, okay.

00:15:22.382 --> 00:15:24.121
And I honestly, I don't have any idea

00:15:24.121 --> 00:15:26.360
how people are perceiving this right now.

00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:27.193
If they're like...

00:15:27.193 --> 00:15:28.026
They're whole...

00:15:28.026 --> 00:15:28.859
If they're like disappointed,
I don't know what it is.

00:15:28.859 --> 00:15:32.791
But like I've always seen
this story of how we met

00:15:32.791 --> 00:15:35.211
as like a comedy routine
that is based in something

00:15:35.211 --> 00:15:36.249
that actually happened,

00:15:36.249 --> 00:15:38.598
but like no standup
comedian who tells the story

00:15:38.598 --> 00:15:40.938
is telling you something
that happened to them

00:15:40.938 --> 00:15:42.495
exactly the way that it happened to them,

00:15:42.495 --> 00:15:44.104
they are taking what happened

00:15:44.104 --> 00:15:47.657
and then they are mythologizing
it in a way to make it funny

00:15:47.657 --> 00:15:51.032
and entertaining because
their job is not a historian,

00:15:51.032 --> 00:15:52.901
their job is a comedian, right.

00:15:52.901 --> 00:15:54.294
Is this argument working?

00:15:54.294 --> 00:15:55.127
And so-

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:57.092
I don't fully buy it.

00:15:57.092 --> 00:15:58.353
But now, but no,

00:15:58.353 --> 00:15:59.542
but now, but so I mean.

00:15:59.542 --> 00:16:00.521
But it is, yeah.

00:16:00.521 --> 00:16:01.386
When a stand up comedian is like,

00:16:01.386 --> 00:16:03.065
listen on the way here...

00:16:03.065 --> 00:16:04.271
And that's a lie, okay.

00:16:04.271 --> 00:16:07.669
If they say that something
just happened to them today,

00:16:07.669 --> 00:16:11.619
100% of the time it did not
happen to them that day, okay.

00:16:11.619 --> 00:16:15.253
If you live in the world and by the way-

00:16:15.253 --> 00:16:16.086
I do live in the world.
Nobody watches

00:16:16.086 --> 00:16:17.714
the the late night shows anymore,

00:16:17.714 --> 00:16:19.237
but if you go on the late...

00:16:19.237 --> 00:16:21.619
If you're on the late night
show and all of a sudden

00:16:21.619 --> 00:16:26.619
the actor has like a funny
story, that's all rehearsed, okay

00:16:26.786 --> 00:16:27.810
it's not like they're just like,

00:16:27.810 --> 00:16:29.401
"You know what, what you just said, Jimmy,

00:16:29.401 --> 00:16:30.776
just made me think of this thing,"

00:16:30.776 --> 00:16:31.952
it's all rehearsed.

00:16:31.952 --> 00:16:33.617
Sorry if you didn't already know that

00:16:33.617 --> 00:16:38.420
but I think that this is
the entertainment version

00:16:38.420 --> 00:16:39.974
of Rhett and Link,

00:16:39.974 --> 00:16:44.946
having a cool packaged
story that is largely true-

00:16:44.946 --> 00:16:46.400
Largely true.

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:47.660
But embellished to a point-
So large.

00:16:47.660 --> 00:16:50.053
To make it snappy and funny.

00:16:50.053 --> 00:16:50.886
Yeah.

00:16:50.886 --> 00:16:51.776
And I mean...

00:16:51.776 --> 00:16:53.917
And at least we're coming out
and saying that's the case.

00:16:53.917 --> 00:16:54.938
And I do think

00:16:54.938 --> 00:16:57.738
there's an evolution of the hypothetical

00:16:57.738 --> 00:17:01.980
to just leaving out the
phrase of the hypothetical

00:17:01.980 --> 00:17:06.305
is just a thing of rhythm
that I'm very good at doing,

00:17:06.305 --> 00:17:07.138
I'm just like,

00:17:07.138 --> 00:17:10.926
you know what? This is a
better way to tell the story,

00:17:10.926 --> 00:17:12.171
it still feels hypothetical

00:17:12.171 --> 00:17:15.251
and then after a while it stops
feeling hypothetical to me.

00:17:15.251 --> 00:17:16.401
Here's the best example of that

00:17:16.401 --> 00:17:17.450
just as a little aside,

00:17:17.450 --> 00:17:19.198
we'll come back to the origin story

00:17:19.198 --> 00:17:20.631
because this just always just crack me up.

00:17:20.631 --> 00:17:21.464
Yeah.

00:17:21.464 --> 00:17:25.193
So, you know our story after
we graduated from college,

00:17:25.193 --> 00:17:26.453
we were engineers from a while

00:17:26.453 --> 00:17:28.789
and then we went on staff with
Campus Crusade For Christ,

00:17:28.789 --> 00:17:31.617
the missionary organization
that we were involved in

00:17:31.617 --> 00:17:32.822
as students, right.

00:17:32.822 --> 00:17:37.283
So we were like college
missionaries for a couple of years

00:17:37.283 --> 00:17:41.126
going around telling people
how to tell people about Jesus,

00:17:41.126 --> 00:17:42.678
right.

00:17:42.678 --> 00:17:45.576
And so, but in order to do that,

00:17:45.576 --> 00:17:46.766
if you're gonna go on staff or crew

00:17:46.766 --> 00:17:48.406
you have to raise support

00:17:48.406 --> 00:17:51.691
which means you have to go
and ask people for money.

00:17:51.691 --> 00:17:53.973
Like sit down with
individuals and families

00:17:53.973 --> 00:17:54.806
and organizations

00:17:54.806 --> 00:17:55.639
and do a presentation.
You do a presentation.

00:17:55.639 --> 00:17:58.519
You go to somebody's home and
you break out your laptop,

00:17:58.519 --> 00:18:00.097
you do a little presentation and you say,

00:18:00.097 --> 00:18:02.915
"So, would you be interested in giving us

00:18:02.915 --> 00:18:05.043
or supporting our mission a $100 a month

00:18:05.043 --> 00:18:05.876
or something like that?"

00:18:05.876 --> 00:18:08.289
Yeah, I had to explain why the two of us

00:18:08.289 --> 00:18:11.872
were gonna be speakers
and seminar creators

00:18:14.145 --> 00:18:17.559
and resident comedians and filmmakers.

00:18:17.559 --> 00:18:19.506
Like, how do you make sense of that?

00:18:19.506 --> 00:18:20.339
Right.

00:18:20.339 --> 00:18:22.031
Well, you talk about the
stories from our past

00:18:22.031 --> 00:18:23.205
of how we did that.

00:18:23.205 --> 00:18:24.038
Right.

00:18:24.038 --> 00:18:24.871
Which we did a lot of that.

00:18:24.871 --> 00:18:25.704
Yeah, yeah.

00:18:25.704 --> 00:18:28.035
But the evolution of how
it came about was like

00:18:28.035 --> 00:18:29.769
right at the time we were raising support

00:18:29.769 --> 00:18:32.612
was when me and you had
become like a comedy duo

00:18:32.612 --> 00:18:35.302
who was like making stuff
together and singing together

00:18:35.302 --> 00:18:37.180
and doing conferences and stuff like that,

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:41.125
but during college I was MCing with Greg.

00:18:41.125 --> 00:18:42.006
As a sidekick.

00:18:42.006 --> 00:18:44.289
And then you were leading
with the worship team.

00:18:44.289 --> 00:18:45.122
Yeah.

00:18:45.122 --> 00:18:45.955
And we weren't doing comedy together,

00:18:45.955 --> 00:18:46.788
we would make video...

00:18:46.788 --> 00:18:48.105
We would make the videos together.

00:18:48.105 --> 00:18:51.026
Like, you would film the videos
of me and Greg and stuff.

00:18:51.026 --> 00:18:52.891
But like that's too complicated to explain

00:18:52.891 --> 00:18:56.211
to a 65 year old dude
who's just sitting there

00:18:56.211 --> 00:18:57.914
falling asleep and just wants to hear you

00:18:57.914 --> 00:18:59.458
tell people about Jesus.

00:18:59.458 --> 00:19:00.291
You know what I'm saying?

00:19:00.291 --> 00:19:01.124
Yeah.

00:19:01.124 --> 00:19:01.957
So you simplify.

00:19:01.957 --> 00:19:02.790
I understand the motivation.

00:19:02.790 --> 00:19:03.623
Greg...

00:19:03.623 --> 00:19:06.141
I became Greg in the
story slowly over time.

00:19:06.141 --> 00:19:06.974
But I...

00:19:06.974 --> 00:19:07.807
But my theory is

00:19:07.807 --> 00:19:09.667
is that after telling
the story a few times

00:19:09.667 --> 00:19:11.784
you believe that to be the case an it was-

00:19:11.784 --> 00:19:12.706
I think Kristy did too.

00:19:13.832 --> 00:19:14.884
'Cause she was there.

00:19:14.884 --> 00:19:16.197
She never said,

00:19:16.197 --> 00:19:17.030
"You know what?

00:19:17.030 --> 00:19:19.374
The story's changed.

00:19:19.374 --> 00:19:21.223
You know, Greg used to be in there,

00:19:21.223 --> 00:19:23.914
now you're just Greg too."

00:19:23.914 --> 00:19:26.965
If we can get a chance to
talk to Greg about this.

00:19:26.965 --> 00:19:27.798
Yeah.

00:19:27.798 --> 00:19:28.631
We-
We need to...

00:19:28.631 --> 00:19:29.464
But, okay.

00:19:29.464 --> 00:19:30.374
But back to the story.

00:19:30.374 --> 00:19:32.092
So you were saying that the-

00:19:32.092 --> 00:19:33.381
So I don't think it was the first day.

00:19:33.381 --> 00:19:34.698
I don't think...

00:19:34.698 --> 00:19:36.792
Ms. Locklear doesn't
think we were held in.

00:19:36.792 --> 00:19:39.091
We know that we weren't writing
nasty words on the desk,

00:19:39.091 --> 00:19:40.493
we don't know what it was.

00:19:40.493 --> 00:19:41.466
I think we got in trouble

00:19:41.466 --> 00:19:45.503
but I think that the coloring
was maybe not the punishment

00:19:45.503 --> 00:19:49.015
but I have a visceral
memory of sitting down

00:19:49.015 --> 00:19:52.533
and watching you coloring
right next to you.

00:19:52.533 --> 00:19:55.844
Always in my mind was just the
two of us in the classroom.

00:19:55.844 --> 00:19:57.864
But I believe the fact...

00:19:57.864 --> 00:20:00.323
The only real fact that I could defend

00:20:00.323 --> 00:20:03.451
is that I once sat next to you and colored

00:20:03.451 --> 00:20:05.861
and made observations about the nature

00:20:05.861 --> 00:20:07.173
of the way you were coloring,

00:20:07.173 --> 00:20:09.267
and I was like, "Wow, he's
like really precise, it's like-

00:20:09.267 --> 00:20:10.100
Mm-hm. Go on.

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:11.258
What is he try...

00:20:11.258 --> 00:20:13.653
Like, I remember thinking like,

00:20:13.653 --> 00:20:14.521
"What is he trying to prove?"

